{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkzL8QwW2UadjEu2oWyu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the self-check and is ready for admission. The smoke fit (100 draws, 1 chain) gave a finite ELPD-LOO of −3563.9.\n\n**What I changed (`streak_weary_chance_pseudoflip`, refining `short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution`):** I added a gambler's-fallacy run-length belief to the incumbent's picture of a fair coin, taken from `gamblers_run_second_order_side_habit`. People believe a coin gets more likely to switch the longer its current streak has run past two flips, by one shared fitted amount per extra flip. That makes a long streak improbable under chance roughly in proportion to the square of its length, so the first one or two breaks of a long streak make a sequence look much more random. This targets the one critique that survives the FDR correction (q = 0.048): in pairs of length 6 or more where both sequences have at most 2 switches, people choose the more-switching sequence 0.872 of the time, against the incumbent's 0.839. The new piece is one parameter (`g_run`) and one computed input (`gam_diff`). Everything else in the incumbent is unchanged.\n\n**Not checked yet:**\n- **Leave-one-out estimate:** the check warned that 6.8% of trials had Pareto k above 0.5, against a 1% tolerance, so this ELPD-LOO may be unreliable. I haven't checked whether that's just the very short smoke fit or whether the incumbent shows the same.\n- **Convergence:** a single chain can't report R-hat, so this is still untested. Admission will test it on the full fit.\n- **Novelty:** the gate could reject the model if the fitted `g_run` comes out near zero, because its predictions would then match the incumbent's.\n- **Speed:** the check took about 18 minutes for its short fit. Admission's full fit stops any sampling run that goes past 30 minutes, so this model may be at risk of being rejected as too slow.\n\nThe files are in `.../experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_4/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2593,"cache_read_input_tokens":98583,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2593,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0268d052-585e-42a5-b281-fc81db63f174","uuid":"5ec81fc6-d7dd-4c72-a3b3-8a8900fa78ee","timestamp":"2026-10-06T12:32:53.978Z","request_id":"req_011CfkzL7zu1spyjCbou4WkS"}
